From: lagz0ne <15101444+lagz0ne@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 08:25:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 32/32] feat(share): a canvas's editors set its link, not only
 its owner

Agents that work over MCP sign in as their own account, so the canvases
they make are theirs: the person they work for is a member and, with
FULL_UI off, never saw Share. Google Docs and Figma let editors share by
default; doop now does too.

canSetLink (server/access.ts) is hasDurableCanvasAccess: the owner, an
invited member or a workspace member may set the link's level and
password (PATCH /api/canvases/:id). Someone in by the link alone, an
account on an open edit link, a link guest or an embedded reviewer, still
gets 403, so a link cannot widen itself. The person's copy of a canvas
carries canSetLink: true (canvas GET, the canvas list, the room init),
and Share (dock, top bar, phone menu, Home's canvas menu) and the
dialog's level picker and password follow it. Invites, moving it to a workspace, deleting it
and the Community listing stay the owner's.

Tests: shareLink.test.ts 'who sets the link' (a member sets level and
password; an account on an edit link and a link guest are refused; the
flag in GET, list and room), access.test.ts updated from owner-only.
